          "text": "The pattern indexes as a primitive cubic cell with \\(a \\approx 4.7852\\) \u00c5. The reflection sequence and intensities are characteristic of the B20 (FeSi-type) structure, space group \\(P2_13\\) (No. 198), with \\(Z=4\\). Representative indexing is 110, 111, 200, 210, 211, 221, 310, 311, 222, 320, 321, and 400.\n\n### Primary structure CIF\n\n```cif\ndata_SiTc_B20\n_audit_creation_method            'Indexed and fitted from supplied Cu Kalpha1 powder pattern'\n_chemical_name_common             'technetium monosilicide'\n_chemical_formula_sum             'Si Tc'\n_chemical_formula_structural      'TcSi'\n_cell_formula_units_Z             4\n\n_space_group_name_H-M_alt         'P 21 3'\n_space_group_IT_number            198\n\n_cell_length_a                     4.7852(3)\n_cell_length_b                     4.7852(3)\n_cell_length_c                     4.7852(3)\n_cell_angle_alpha                 90\n_cell_angle_beta                  90\n_cell_angle_gamma                 90\n_cell_volume                      109.572(20)\n\n_exptl_crystal_density_diffrn      7.64\n\nloop_\n_atom_type_symbol\n_atom_type_oxidation_number\nTc  0\nSi  0\n\nloop_\n_atom_site_label\n_atom_site_type_symbol\n_atom_site_symmetry_multiplicity\n_atom_site_Wyckoff_symbol\n_atom_site_fract_x\n_atom_site_fract_y\n_atom_site_fract_z\n_atom_site_occupancy\nTc1  Tc  4  a  0.136(3)  0.136(3)  0.136(3)  1.0\nSi1  Si  4  a  0.844(3)  0.844(3)  0.844(3)  1.0\n```\n\nThe ordinary powder pattern cannot determine the absolute structural hand. The inversion-related B20 model, obtained by replacing each coordinate \\(x\\) with \\(1-x\\), is diffraction-equivalent: approximately Tc at \\((0.864,0.864,0.864)\\) and Si at \\((0.156,0.156,0.156)\\). No distinct non-B20 alternative survives the observed peak positions and systematic intensity distribution.",
